# ProofRun site credentials (Class C) — organizer-provided, per batch. See docs/SPEC.md §11.2
#
# Import on the VM (CLI only, no web upload):
#   python -m orchestrator.cli vault import site-credentials.env     # validates, encrypts, prints aliases only, offers to shred the file
#   python -m orchestrator.cli vault list                             # aliases, domains, expiry — never values
#   python -m orchestrator.cli vault purge --all
#
# Rules: values are encrypted at rest, never shown to any LLM, never placed in a container that runs submission code,
# scrubbed from logs/receipts, and every use is recorded as (alias, domain, time).
# Naming: <KIND>_<ALIAS>_<FIELD>=value   KIND = SITE | API   ALIAS = A-Z0-9, 2–32 chars. Unknown fields are rejected.

# ---- SITE: a website login typed by the trusted browser harness (Mode L, P1) ----
# The Prober only writes:  await pr.login("TEAM42")
# The harness fills the form ONLY if the page origin is exactly https://<DOMAIN>. SSO/CAPTCHA/2FA → stops, needs a human.
SITE_TEAM42_DOMAIN=demo.team42.app
SITE_TEAM42_LOGIN_URL=https://demo.team42.app/login
SITE_TEAM42_USERNAME=judge-test@example.com
SITE_TEAM42_PASSWORD=change-me
# Submission ids allowed to use this credential, or *
SITE_TEAM42_JOBS=team42
SITE_TEAM42_EXPIRES=2026-11-10
# Optional, if auto-detection of the form fails:
# SITE_TEAM42_USER_SELECTOR=input[name=email]
# SITE_TEAM42_PASS_SELECTOR=input[type=password]
# SITE_TEAM42_SUBMIT_SELECTOR=button[type=submit]

# ---- API: a key a submission needs to run from its repo (Mode R, P2 broker — not in P0) ----
# The sandbox only ever sees a placeholder in NASA_API_KEY; the egress broker swaps in the real value
# only for requests to DOMAIN. Until P2 ships, such submissions are tiered ⚫ "Needs secrets".
API_NASA_DOMAIN=api.nasa.gov
API_NASA_ENV=NASA_API_KEY
API_NASA_VALUE=change-me
# query:<param> | header:<Name> | header:Authorization:Bearer
API_NASA_INJECT=query:api_key
API_NASA_JOBS=*
API_NASA_EXPIRES=2026-11-10
